    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d86">

                <pb facs="0273" n="149" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg149"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00 R 294/148: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Herrick</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-03-26T19:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 26,
                                1923—7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>121. For Wadsworth. W–13. Your W–12, March 26.</p>
                <p>The fixation of interest on deficits of the 12 annual installments at 4¼% is
                    suggested. This is the average rate here and is also the rate payable on the
                    three years’ arrears of interest on the debt of Great Britain. If you should
                    find it desirable, however, you may agree to a 4% interest rate.</p>
                <p>In reply to your W–14<anchor n="99" xml:id="d86-f1"/> you should send any further
                    suggestions that in your opinion should be considered by this Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
